      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the body say what goes wrong without this patch? As far as I can see, a driver that sizes the remap in kernel pages, for example `PAGE_SIZE` for a 4KB VMA, makes `remap_pfn_range()` install PTEs past `vm_end`, and `remap_pte_range()` hits `BUG_ON(!pte_none())` when the next mapping already has a PTE there. If the `vm_slice_off` check stays, it needs its own reason as well.\n\nMaybe something like:\n\n```\nANDROID: P3S: mm: Clamp remap_pfn_range() to the VMA in 4KB processes\n\nA driver that sizes remap_pfn_range() in kernel pages, such as\nPAGE_SIZE or PAGE_ALIGN(len), asks for whole 16KB pages. When a 4KB\nVMA ends partway through one, remap_pfn_range() installs PTEs past\nvm_end, outside the VMA, and hits BUG_ON(!pte_none()) in\nremap_pte_range() if the next mapping already has a PTE there.\n\nTrim a request that ends in the unused slices of the VMA\u0027s last kernel\npage to vm_end, and reject one that reaches beyond that page, before\nchanging any PTE.\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "ac03d343a247a96cb219f705f66184ab63272f40",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
