      "message": "Would you mind moving the `vma_is_p3s_4k()` check into `p3s_remap_pfn_range_size()`, returning 0 for native VMAs as `p3s_fork_widen_range()` does in the same header? Then `remap_pfn_range_notrack()` keeps a single hook:\n\n```\n\tint error \u003d p3s_remap_pfn_range_size(vma, addr, \u0026size);\n\n\tif (error)\n\t\treturn error;\n\terror \u003d remap_pfn_range_internal(vma, addr, pfn, size, prot);\n```\n\nI think `P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM()` can go as well. As far as I can see, nothing in this function reads `PAGE_SIZE`: the helper uses the `_4KB` constants, and `remap_pfn_range_internal()` and `unmap_page_range()` set the context themselves. `mm/p3s/memory.h` builds without P3S too, so no stub is needed.",
