      "message": "Thanks, the reason in the commit message makes sense to me, since `remap_pfn_range()` can\u0027t tell which callers handle `vm_slice_off`.\n\nCould the refusal go through `p3s_4k_unsupported()`, as `p3s_vm_iomap_memory()` does in aosp/4368009? Then a 4KB app whose `mmap()` fails here shows up in the log, and we\u0027d notice if the check turns away a caller that handles the slice, such as `system_heap_mmap()`. Something like:\n\n```\n\tif (vma_slice_off(vma) \u0026\u0026 p3s_4k_unsupported(vma-\u003evm_mm))\n\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n```\n\nwith `vma_slice_off(vma)` dropped from the check below.",
